# NPM Library Standards

Every export is a **forever promise**. Consumer-first, explicit, minimal surface, semver-safe.

## Public API

- Export only from `src/index.ts`; mark internals `/** @internal */`
- Named exports only; explicit `exports` map in `package.json`
- Options-object pattern for 3+ parameters; explicit return types on public functions
- Typed errors (`EngineConfigError`, etc.) — not generic `Error`
- `peerDependencies` for React — never bundle React in `dependencies`
- `sideEffects: false` unless documented exceptions

## Naming & files

- Files: `kebab-case.ts`; tests: `*.test.ts`, `*.test-d.ts`
- No abbreviations (`cb`, `fn`, `err`, `res`, `ctx`, `idx`)
- Booleans: `is` / `has` / `can` / `should` prefix
- Interfaces: PascalCase, no `I` prefix; hooks: `use` prefix

## Code quality

- No `console.log` in library source (init-time config warnings are the documented exception)
- No `any`; `unknown` at boundaries with narrowing
- Pure render-pipeline stages — no mutating stage inputs
- JSDoc required on public exports: `@param`, `@returns`, `@throws`, `@example`, `@since`

## Tests & release

- Unit per layer; integration for plugin lifecycle, schema cascade, render pipeline, consumer simulation
- Type tests (`tsd` / `expect-type`) for public API
- CI: lint (zero warnings), typecheck, test, build, size budget

